  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Nine apps \u00b7 six backend owners",
      "items": [
        "Contacts manages staff identities and application access. Calendar owns school dates, parity and events. Deploy owns planning/publication; Layout shares its backend and physical room register.",
        "Roster owns baseline, suspended and relief timetable state. Venues owns room bookings and facilities permissions. LORD, OVERLORD and STARLORD share one booking/device backend."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Identity and source exchanges",
      "items": [
        "Private staff apps retain Google sign-in/session checks. STARLORD keeps its read-only display model and separate outer access policy. Venues also supports verified Access JWTs; its backend resolves active Contacts identity and facilities grants.",
        "Roster reads Contacts authority over a signed bridge and published Deploy quota/catalogue through read-only workbook access; its gateway gets Calendar date context. LORD refreshes signed Contacts/Deploy manifests. Venues reads signed Contacts, Deploy/Layout, Calendar and Roster projections."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Venues admission and timetable precedence",
      "items": [
        "A signed Roster begin creates a durable Venues fence before occupancy-changing timetable writes. Unrelated absence and audit work can continue. Complete marks the source stale; sync activates only when captured revisions and fence tokens still match.",
        "Server validation checks current permissions, date coverage, room rules, pending holds, closures and effective timetable occupancy. Booking/transfer effects, audit, receipt and notification intent commit together in the Venues workbook. No cross-service atomicity is claimed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Stores, delivery and maintenance",
      "items": [
        "Each Apps Script project owns its mutable records and locking. Roster retains Drive JSON; Venues uses atomic Sheets batch updates and immutable Drive occupancy pieces. Browser caches accelerate reads but never authorize a write.",
        "The Roster Worker claims durable intents; optional Queue messages only wake it. Optional R2/D1 serve documented Roster media, snapshots and webhook jobs. LORD and Venues dispatch their own notifications. Uncertain provider acceptance requires review.",
        "This source map is a companion to README.md, the deployment authority. It describes repository contracts, not a live infrastructure audit. See the editable Draw.io pages and evidence JSON for exact source ownership."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Local source evidence",
      "items": [
        "Source identity: local GSiS_v0.9_Correction_Source_History.bundle. No hosted upstream is asserted. The pinned revision, source ranges and file hashes are retained in architecture-evidence.json and architecture-source.json; architecture-text.md is the text alternative.",
        "Archify cannot verify local-bundle origins. Its passing gates cover the rendered artifact and browser behavior; repository provenance is checked separately against local Git objects. README.md remains the only deployment guide."
      ]
    }
  ]
